[00:15.16] I was a highwayman, along the coach roads I did ride
[00:21.08] With sword and pistol by my side
[00:26.80] Many a young maid lost her baubles to my trade
[00:32.30] Many a soldier shed his life blood on my blade
[00:38.52] The bastards hung me in the spring of '25
[00:44.08] But I am still alive
[00:50.94] I was a sailor, I was born upon the tide
[00:57.06] And with the sea I did abide
[01:02.00] I sailed a schooner 'round the horn to Mexico
[01:07.78] I went aloft to furl the mainsail in a blow
[01:13.20] And when the yards broke off, they said that I got killed
[01:19.38] But I am living still
[01:26.64] I was a dam builder across the river deep and wide
[01:31.66] Where steel and water did collide
[01:38.16] A place called Boulder on the wild Colorado
[01:43.88] I slipped and fell into the wet concrete below
[01:49.66] They buried me in that gray tomb that knows no sound
[01:55.00] But I am still around
[01:58.34] I'll always be around and around and around
[02:03.72] And around and around and around
[02:12.96] I'll fly a star ship across the universe divide
[02:19.22] And when I reach the other side
[02:25.50] I'll find a place to rest my spirit if I can
[02:29.34] Perhaps I may become a highwayman again
[02:36.20] Or I may simply be a single drop of rain
[02:42.08] But I will remain
[02:45.86] And I'll be back again and again and again
[02:50.64] And again and again and again
